WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
 Pierre would not let this opportunity go by without trying to sell you

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.000
 something.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
 Daniel 48 anniversary is being celebrated this coming Friday.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.830
 Pierre, whenever I make it to the White House as president, you will be my

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.000
 speech writer.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
 Thank you very kindly.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
 You know, nice people, God, that's America before I start anything else.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
 And I really mean it when I say that.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.280
 We all came from different parts of the world, our families came from different

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.000
 parts of the world.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000
 And we assembled in peace and lovely camaraderie and so on.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
 We're not afraid of the police or whatever it is.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
 How do you defense the battery of this one?

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
 Thank you, sir.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
 I just a couple of years ago, they told me I was trying to take notice.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.000
 I had no idea what that is.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.330
 So that's why I came with you because I'm coward when it comes to servers and

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.000
 all that stuff.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
 Okay, that's just how it is.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.000
 And God bless them.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
 They told me, there's not a way out of me, Abby.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
 It's just, if some anecdote, three minutes.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
 He said three minutes.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
 I can't tell you my name.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.010
 I want to thank all the committees and everyone who is involved in this great

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.000
 endeavor.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.160
 Cleveland is like great as an intervention and I love it to read the small

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:44.490
 paragraph that I received from the president of my University of Richmond,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.000
 Virginia.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
 I had no idea I knew about this.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:56.000
 And it came to my heart.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.340
 I want to thank all the committees and everyone who is involved in this great

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.000
 endeavor.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.160
 Cleveland is like great as an intervention and I love it to read the small

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:10.920
 paragraph that I received from the president of my University of Richmond,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.000
 Virginia.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.000
 I had no idea I knew about this.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.390
 Abby, I write with immense pride to congratulate on being inducted into the

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.000
 Cleveland International Hall of Fame.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.220
 I'm so pleased that this honor has been bestowed upon you and I'm grateful that

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:35.000
 your commitment to diversity and inclusion has strengthened the multicultural

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.000
 vibrancy of Cleveland.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.000
 Some nice words like that about the president of the University.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.000
 I want to thank also Mr. Mike Miller. Thank you very kindly, sir.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.000
 And I want to thank all the friends that showed up here that came.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
 We have relatives that came here from Virginia.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.260
 We have good friends that came here from Canton, Ohio, from Akron, from Toledo,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.000
 from all over the place.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.000
 This means this organization is so credible.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.340
 Thank you, everybody. You know what? Next year, maybe you'll hold the meeting

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.000
 and join Daddy and Rocket League.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.000
 There you go.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.920
 Really, I didn't want you to bother and come here this evening, but if you didn't

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.000
 show up, I would have felt bad too.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:33.000
 Your brother's here warms my heart. I appreciate that.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.000
 I love you.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:41.670
 Thank you. I was born in a little town called Pafreya, which is now famous for

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.000
 the National drink, hot and wine.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:49.000
 It reminds me of the orders of Mary Burek.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.000
 What's the name?

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.000
 Andy here for thank you, except they had the...

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.000
 What do you call it?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
 Who would let that cook?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.000
 Okay, but now the town is very prosperous. People are very well educated.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
 I was there last September.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.000
 You have to watch out for the cars when you cross the road.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:15.000
 We were written on a street exactly, on a road, and the town is very good.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.260
 So in the 1950s, my uncle, Joe Weiner from New Pernice, Virginia, is my father's

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.000
 brother,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.890
 and his daughter is here with us, and his grandson is here, and I appreciate

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.000
 that coming here.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.030
 He visited us at 11, and he said, "Son, did you want to go to America as a

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.000
 student?"

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:39.000
 I said, "Give me time to think about half a second."

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.000
 I said, "Of course. I'll tell you never to ask."

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.140
 So I came here to New Pernice for one year, then the University of Richmond,

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.000
 Virginia.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.000
 A beautiful experience happened to me at the University of Richmond. A kid, a

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:57.000
 college kid.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:19.300
 Wayne Arder from Fred

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.300
 from New Pernice. He said, "No, you can have it."

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.300
 "No, I have it. You can have it."

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.300
 I was happy that I finally accepted you.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:33.390
 I know he asked. He said, "You know what, Debbie? I just, I don't know how you're

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.300
 going to impress me very well."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.790
 He impressed me really. He said, "We just got engaged. Next year, when we get

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:43.300
 married, I would like for her to be my best man."

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:47.300
 I said, "What do they do?" I said, "I don't know."

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.770
 He said, "We're between now and then, everybody's fine out." That's what

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.300
 happened.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:57.300
 We became friends and he called me after 50, 60 years or something like that

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.300
 from Texas.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.300
 So this is a wonderful experience.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:08.300
 And to me, the fact that I studied in Islamic schools, Catholic schools,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.300
 Protestant schools, secular schools.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:18.430
 If you thought there are two sides to every story, there are five, six, seven

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.300
 sides to every story.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:25.670
 But I don't respect that. Love and beauty. All we have to do in life, most of

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.300
 the time, is just to listen to each other.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:36.300
 Don't interrupt each other all the time.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:41.560
 So I thought maybe, maybe, maybe, conversations on us guys, people, I mean,

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.300
 people, should be like dragging on a highway.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:51.390
 There's a time to eat, a time to stop, a time to, you know, but no records to

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.300
 drive.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.300
 Anyhow, at the University of Richmond, I really got involved in everything.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:04.910
 As a student of government and so on, in the newspaper, I became editor of the

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:09.300
 literary newspaper, it's called The Messenger.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.480
 I had some proclivity, I gotta tell you this, with all the honesty, with all

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:18.480
 the humility, to writing and this narrative and love and writing in English and

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.300
 under two bread.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:25.110
 Except when I came back here, I lost my southern Lebanese accent, adopted a

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.300
 Cleveland accent again.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:33.300
 I got to Cleveland. By the way, I wanted to live in Virginia.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.090
 We got married being what my wife known of, been married for 55 years, as

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.300
 Pierre mentioned.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:44.410
 That was a miserable year for the weather. What should I do? We got married in

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:45.300
 November.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:50.810
 I said, "I think we're going to Virginia." She said, "Let's try it for a year,

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.300
 huh? If you don't like it, we'll go back."

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.300
 And I was still trying it.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.300
 [Laughter]

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:04.280
 So, anyhow, apply for the job, because some of you, if you read it, I work for

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.300
 Blue Cross.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:13.370
 Apply for the job. I answered an ad in the paper. It says, "Savings and

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.300
 investment."

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.090
 I said, "That's a nice and clean job." I had no idea what the insurance was

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.300
 talking about.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:27.320
 They gave a subject to memorize. Until about maybe three weeks after that, I

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.300
 figured, "What? Take this insurance. I don't want insurance."

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:34.300
 Anyhow, I set it into it, because I don't like to move around.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.980
 So, Pierre mentioned about Cameo, even American

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:41.040
 media organization. I got involved with that. I have met one of the boys with a

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.300
 lot of details.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:48.680
 And I love America so much. It bothered me from the college days to see

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.300
 somebody who can spend years here in America,

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:57.300
 and they have no idea what America is all about, really. I'm not as color about

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.300
 American history, but I studied American history very well.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:08.070
 And through Cameo, I started telling the people in our readings, whatever they

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:08.300
 go,

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:16.300
 "If you're planning to stay in this country here, you should be a citizen."

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:21.850
 And I teach you to become a citizen. When I teach in English and Arabic, and

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.300
 when my radio program came along,

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:31.400
 I started teaching them that on the radio. The questions and the answers, and

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.300
 every time I put a bit of history in it,

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:37.900
 so that it's so true in the hand. They appreciated that very much. That's why

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.300
 the immigration people gave me a little

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:48.750
 bit of a citation for that, and I also appreciate that. And for one thing, I

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:54.300
 know people don't vote sometimes, because we're almost done voting, because

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:54.300
 they don't know how.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.390
 They're afraid of that machine. We either rented, but our members rented or

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:02.300
 bought or did something with a voting machine,

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:06.580
 and we took it during our picnic. And I try to be, don't be afraid, I'm afraid

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.300
 of it too. Nobody's going to bother you.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.920
 You put this paper right here, you wanted to talk to it, you wanted to vote to

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.300
 it, to time, you pushed this button here to vote to it.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:21.590
 You don't make it very easy for them. And that had tremendous effect on the

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:22.300
 people.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:28.300
 Again, when I had my radio show, the radio show was a learning instrument also.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:34.300
 I love Arabic, I love English, I love history.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:38.160
 I was telling them also the questions and answers, making it easy, how to

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:43.300
 become a citizen. And many times I accompanied them to become a citizen.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:48.300
 I love this nation, and we have to do whatever we can to keep it number one.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:54.300
 [applause]

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.880
 And that's why we're not too bad about it. Because there's no other nation in

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:02.300
 the world that did to the world as much good as this country did.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:09.300
 And as I used to mention on the radio, what else would you rather live? Tell me.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:10.300
 I believe you can tell me.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:14.010
 I don't mean you go on vacation to this mother nation or that place. I mean to

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:18.300
 live, where would you rather live? Right here.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.300
 And do you even know how you serve to live?

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.300
 [laughter]

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:28.260
 Good thanks to everyone. I want to also mention Father Naheu from my church. He's

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:32.300
 a friend and a pastor. Well, thank you very much.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:37.300
 [applause]

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.300
 And his mother also, Mrs. Samira.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.300
 [applause]

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:50.250
 You're very kind. I appreciate that. I consider you my family also. I have two

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:53.300
 beautiful faces, beautiful people.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:58.300
 Thank you for coming. I appreciate that. You've been very kind. Thank you.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.300
 [applause]

